# Revisions ignored by `git blame`.
#
# Bulk mechanical commits only — a formatting sweep, a mass rename, a pure move.
# A commit that also changed behaviour must NEVER be listed here: blame would then
# hide a real change, which is worse than the noise this file removes.
# See 23-git-workflow-hooks-and-commits.md and
# 30-restructuring-an-existing-react-project.md ("Protect the history you are about
# to churn"), whose R-2 this file is the practical enforcement of.
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# ENABLE IT — this file does nothing until you run this once, per clone:
#
#     git config blame.ignoreRevsFile .git-blame-ignore-revs
#
# It is local config and does not clone, exactly like core.hooksPath.
# GitHub and GitLab apply a root-level .git-blame-ignore-revs automatically in
# their blame views; your local `git blame` does not until you run the line above.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# LOCATION: this file lives at the GIT ROOT, shared by all four components, per
# 23-git-workflow-hooks-and-commits.md ("create it before the first bulk commit, at
# the git root, shared by all four components"). It is deliberately NOT in frontend/:
# blame.ignoreRevsFile is a single repo-level config value and forge auto-detection
# only reads the repo root, so a copy inside a component directory would be inert.
#
# FORMAT: one full 40-character SHA per line, with a comment naming the commit.
# Add the SHA in the SAME commit that performs the sweep is impossible (the SHA does
# not exist yet), so add it in the immediately following commit and say so.
#
# Example:
#   # chore(frontend): apply prettier formatting baseline
#   0000000000000000000000000000000000000000
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
